#
# TWRP-format flags for jason (Xiaomi Mi Note 3).
#
# /etc/recovery.fstab has to stay in the plain AOSP five-column format because
# libfs_mgr parses it too (the FBE code calls ReadDefaultFstab(); with the old
# TWRP format it fails and decryption becomes impossible). This file is read only
# by the recovery: TWPartitionManager::Process_Fstab() loads /etc/twrp.flags into
# a map, applies the flags to the entries it finds in recovery.fstab, and then
# adds every mount point that exists only here as an extra partition.
#
# That is how the OrangeFox ground rules
#
#   B. USB OTG must be mounted as "/usb_otg" with a display flag of "USB-Storage"
#   C. the fstab must provide for backup of internal storage (as "/storage")
#
# are satisfied without breaking libfs_mgr. This device has no MicroSD slot, so
# rule A (/sdcard1) does not apply, and it has no dynamic partitions, so
# /system_image and /vendor_image (cust) carry backup=1;flashimg=1 in
# recovery.fstab as rule D requires.
#
# <mount point>  <fstype>  <block device>   [alternate block device]  flags=...
/usb_otg          vfat      /dev/block/sda1  /dev/block/sda            flags=fsflags=utf8;display="USB-Storage";storage;wipeingui;removable
/storage          ext4      /data/media/0    flags=display="Internal Storage";usermrf;backup=1;fsflags="bind";removable
